    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>362 Riverside Drive, Apt. 8-D <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319"
                            type="place">New York</rs> 25, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__865"
                            type="place">N. Y.</rs>
                        <lb/><date when="1946-08-19">August 19, 1946</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <fw place="top-left" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Dr. Paul J. Tillich</rs>
                        <lb/>P. O. Box 1419 <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__769" type="place">East
                            Hampton</rs>, Long Island</fw>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr.
                        Tillich</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>As one of your students who numbers himself among a host of your admirers, allow
                    me to extend to you most heartly congratulations and felicitations upon the
                    occasion of your sixtieth birthday.</p>
                <p>It is with a sincere desire to express my personal appreciation of your work as a
                    teacher and as an author that I join the many who would like to acknowledge
                    their debt to you as one whose thought has been, and will continue to be, the
                    source of greatest inspiration in the vocation of the Christian ministry.</p>
                <p>Not only do I rejoice in the opportunity that has been mine to have studied under
                    you, but look forward eagerly to the contributions you will make in the years to
                    come.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>Most Sincerely yours,</salute>
                    <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3865" type="person">Paul C. Hayner</rs>
                        <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3865" type="person">Paul C. Hayner</rs>.
                        <!-- Unterschrift, dann gedruckt. --></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
